{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The multimeter fits my breadboards, relay modules, and PCB parts because it would help me check power, wiring, and continuity while building circuits.",
    "The electronic cleaner and caliper support the same hands-on work: maintaining contacts and measuring components or mounting clearances."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The filaments and printer bed assume I own a 3D printer, but my electronics purchases do not establish that equipment or a printing project.",
    "The fuel can and large installation supports serve tasks I have not shown a need for, while twelve tubes of glue exceed any bonding need I currently have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in making and repairing things seems to have been stretched into an interest in 3D printing and its supplies.",
    "My hardware purchases seem to have been treated as evidence that any workshop supply would be useful, regardless of the task or scale."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My breadboards, relay, battery holder, and PCB supplies point toward small circuit assembly and troubleshooting, which makes electrical testing tools especially relevant.",
    "I need a concrete use for an item now; specialized supplies depend on equipment I actually own, and bulk quantities need a specific project to justify them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my electronics work but extended it too broadly into unrelated workshop tasks and unestablished 3D printing needs."
}"}
